    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "makes sense. what about the cost though? is the shinkansen way more expensive than flying domestic, or is it pretty comparable if i'm booking a bit in advance? also any advice on how to handle the transfers between stations and hotels so i don't waste too much time?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Cost-wise, it's a bit of a toss-up, but if you book your Shinkansen tickets well in advance, especially if you look into a Japan Rail Pass or specific discounted fares, it can become quite competitive with domestic flights. For your travel between cities, the Shinkansen is usually more predictable in its cost structure than juggling flight prices, which can change suddenly. To minimize travel time between stations and hotels, pre-book accommodation that is very close to major train stations, like a central JR station. This saves you the time of navigating local transit from a distant hotel.",
      "source": "target",
